{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes","id":1494974,"title":"Thoughts on W5 tribes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-14T10:39:24-07:00","id":1494974,"title":"Thoughts on W5 tribes","content":"<u><b>This is not a thread about if the wholesale changes are good or not, this thread is focused on the tribes and what flaws I have seen as they are presented in the preview and Justin's comments.</b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Black Furies-</b> Furies might be a tribe prone to fighting, but I feel they would serve better as a Wisdom tribe. Once you get past the angry young Furies, the tribe has a lot more spiritual stuff than stuff dedicated to combat. A larger flaw I see is the inclusion of men into the tribe. Furies are a tribe focused on the mysteries of womanhood and the deeper concept of the Earth Mother as a mother. If this concept does not fit W5, I would have preferred the Furies to be omitted than changed like this.<br /> <br /> Their updated glyph is all right, though I liked the original more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bone Gnawers- </b>The only two issues I see here are the tribe being listed as a tribe of Honour and the implication that you can now be a rich Bone Gnawer. Even the Gnawer verbs hint that the tribe is not exactly honourable. The Gnawers are a tribe tied to being in the worst places and thriving, things like Honour and dignity do not go with it. The tribe name and totem HIGHLY also imply they are not a tribe of manners. The best renown to tie to the Gnawers should be Glory.<br /> <br /> <b>Children of Gaia- </b>The Coggies should be a tribe of Honour, as they more or less hold a leadership position.<br /> <br /> <b>Fianna- </b>Maybe a name change. Otherwise, I don't see anything worth changing.<br /> <br /> <b>Galestalkers- </b>Change the Ban to something not related to eating meat. The name change and the totem change are fine and needed.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost Council- </b>Nothing worth commenting on from me.<br /> <br /> <b>Glass Walkers- </b>Why did their tribe patron change to the spider? What was wrong with the cockroach?<br /> <br /> <b>Red Talons-</b> The Talons also suffer from the push for inclusivity and a mismatched renown type. But I think as a tribe, they should have been cut entirely. I like the Talons, but over the years I have gotten the message loud and clear that most people don't like Talons, see them as disruptive to their games and just generally only good for NPCs at best. There is a reason why in Forsaken the Predator Kings (a tribe clearly based on the Red Talons) were made an antagonist tribe.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Lords- </b>They should be a tribe of Honour, not Glory. Also, what IS their new glyph supposed to be?<br /> <br /> <b>Silent Striders- N</b>othing much to comment on, their new glyph looks fine.<br /> <br /> <b>Silver Fangs- </b>From what I understand, the focus of W5 is very low level and the characters are struggling to survive. In that setting, the Silver Fangs make very little sense. The tribe is defined by their rulership and also their inner corruption. This tribe could be better used as an antagonist (and was in Forsaken.) Their new glyph is fine.<br /> <br /> These are just my thoughts on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T12:19:40-07:00","id":1494980,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about how to make sense of the choices of verbs and what they say about how the Tribes are portrayed. And this is what I came up with:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Glory</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Honor</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Wisdom</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Stealth</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Shadow Lords</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Bone Gnawers</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Glass Walkers</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Fight/Confront</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Black Furies</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Galestalkers</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Ghost Council</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Community</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">(Get of Fenris)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Silver Fangs</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Silent Striders</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Protect</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Fianna</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Red Talons</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Children Of Gaia</td> </tr> </table></div> Now the logic here is that there are two traits: The Renown and a specific way to express the Renown. The way I got the four categories on the left is:<ul><li>Stealth are Tribes that have verbs about doing things secretly or using subterfuge (SL: scheme, BG: Eavesdrop, GW: Hack)</li> <li>Fight/Confront are Tribes that look to engage enemies (BF: Overcome/Demolish, Gale: Ambush, GhoC: Subvert)</li> <li>Community are Tribes that do something that benefits other Garou (SF: Inspire, SiSt: Deliver (ie being messengers))</li> <li>Protect are Tribes that have verbs for defending (Fi: Protect, RT: Ward, CoG: Heal)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Now as for Renowns, I think there are also similarities:<ul><li>Glory Tribes have aspirational verbs about achieving some future goal (SL: Envision, BF: Avenge, Fi: Reclaim)</li> <li>Honor Tribes are about contributing a service to Garou society (BG: Witness, GS: Track (ie tracking down enemies), SF: Motivate, RT: Purge)</li> <li>Wisdom Tribes deal with the occult secrets of the world (including the Umbra) (GW: Research, GhoC: Unearth, SiSt: Scout, CoG: Puzzle Out)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> Not 100% sure about all of this but that's how I could envision what the new Tribes are like in W5. And I'm not really sure how to make this work without changing some Tribes massively.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T13:20:32-07:00","id":1494982,"title":"","content":"<b>Black Furies-</b> Personally I'm fine with the change to include men, I also don't really have a problem if their more geared to the tearing down of old to find new, which is what they seem to be. (Avenge, Overcome, Dismantle, Demolish.) I think that is a different take on them for sure but, I don't think it's bad.<br /> <br /> <b>Glasswalkers-</b> I really want to know why its spider and how affects them. It really makes me feel like at one point there was a chart that on one side had the renown and on the other had the triant. So the Weaver-Wisdom Tribe was the Glasswalkers so their Parton was Spider. I have no base for this just seems like at one point it was in the design. (Also why Wyld-Glory is Black Furies) <br /> <br /> <b>Red Talons-</b> I think these also need another pass. With the verbs of 'Ruin' and 'Purge' it seems like they are <i>off</i>. Like Ward is good and Reduce is Ok. Again we have Black Furies over here with 'Dismantle' and 'Demolish' which are pretty close to the same but slightly different in terms of negative connation. 'I'm going to ruin this house' and 'I'm going to dismantle this house' mean the same thing but are very different in how you perceive them. <br /> <br /> <b>Gale Stalkers, Ghost Council-</b> I think both of these need another pass or just not be included. If you are saying that in your redesign that no tribe was <i>ever</i> restricted to a geographical location and instead all tribes are found everywhere then why even have these obviously Native American coded tribes. <br /> <br /> <b>Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, Fianna, Shadow Lords, Silent Striders, Silver Fangs -</b> Seem the same to me, I have no issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T14:44:05-07:00","id":1494985,"title":"","content":"Where are you lot reading updates on new tribe changes?<br /> <br /> <br /> Putting tribes into honour/wisdom/glory types seems far too reductionist and is far more the province of auspices. It's especially confusing when we're using terms that could be used three ways: A human, a bone gnawer and a black fury have very different ideas on what &quot;wisdom&quot; is after all. The Black Furies might be particularly adept at dealing with certain spirits but their players at my tables have a tendency towards sub-par decisions.<br /> <br /> <b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Glass Walkers- </div> </div> </div></b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why did their tribe patron change to the spider? What was wrong with the cockroach? </div> </div> </div>0/10 fell to weaver just because they wanted a more recognizably popular totem. Next thing they're going to say whippoorwill isn't recognizably edgy enough so BSDs will get snakes or wasps or scorpions or some shit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T14:46:51-07:00","id":1494986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1494985#post1494985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are you lot reading updates on new tribe changes?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/werewolf-the-apocalypse-tribes-and-renown\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news...bes-and-renown</a> Here","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T15:29:48-07:00","id":1494989,"title":"","content":"I always wondered by the Bone Gnawers couldn't be rich and HAD to be poor. Was it meant to be a Ban from their Totem? I never saw that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T15:38:02-07:00","id":1494990,"title":"","content":"OK.<br /> <br /> So first off some general thoughts that go beyond each Tribe by itself:<br /> <br /> With our current level of information, there's just too many Tribes. It's obviously they want to keep the original set in the setting (even if not all of them playable or in the core book anyway), but there's so many changes going on why some things are deemed important to keep and others aren't is hard to wrap your head around. Without something that more obviously delineates each Tribe's game-function to replace the ethno-geographic-cultural links that separated them before, it's very unclear why global anyone-can-in-theory-join organizations have so much overlap.<br /> <br /> Conversely, there are too few Renown traits for this setup. Lots of them make sense, some don't make sense based on assumptions about how those Tribes were in the past but could make sense if the Tribe are heavily redone, and others seem very hard to justify no matter how you reinvision the Tribe (esp. without making the previous point worse). Long before W5 was even something anyone was thinking about, we had threads about three Renown categories not being enough just on how the old Renown setup really screwed over Galliards that didn't act like back-up Ahrouns (Galliards had a high Glory requirement, which makes a high-concept level of sense, but the books made the non-combat sources of Glory via inspiration, storytelling, etc. pittances in comparison).<br /> <br /> The Favor/Ban thing sounds fine in the theory, but we need more examples. It's also hard to judge them without more examples, and knowing what the new Gifts look like and if Rites are even a mechanical thing. The Shadow Lord favor feels very lack luster if assumptions around what Theurges did in the past remain remotely viable. Even if we look past the glaring issue of North Wind being attached to the replacement Tribe for Younger Brother, it seems like one of those things that's basically either never real problem, or a gigantic pain in the ass,as it doesn't seem to have any dials attached to it (a common problem in the old WtA Tribe flaws). Again though there's glaring holes in what we know. How bad is it to break a ban? Is W5 moving the Garou in a similar direction as the Uratha where all of them have to hunt regularly and become more strict carnivores over time, thus North Wind is just making an aspect of that worse? Or is it really just going to stand out like a hangnail compared to the rest?<br /> <br /> In general the glyph redesigns feel like change for change's sake. The Gnawer one is the only one that's an improvement to me (and it's just more legible now), the rest are either minor changes that don't seem to add anything, or overt changes I don't understand. It feels like there's a lack of interest in the glyphs as part of an overarching communication system though. The changes to the Clan icons and addition of Discipline ones in V5 is generally fine, because there isn't the implication that they're regular parts of vampire culture. You can imagine that vampires might slip such designs into larger ones as claims or threats normal people wouldn't get (&quot;Hey, neonate, don't just go in there, look close, you can tell that's a Malkavian's place, and they're announcing that they're using Auspex to spy on people that go in&quot;) but you wouldn't expect those designs to be carved into trees or stones to relate more complex ideas.<br /> <br /> By Tribe:<br /> <br /> Black Furies - We just don't know enough about how they're being handled in the light of what else we know. I'm not opposed to them being slightly less radical feminist (I kind of liked how BNS WtA capped Rank for male Furies as it leans into the idea that membership isn't the same as equality), but we really need to see how the Tribe of Gorgon operates in this new context. Glory doesn't bother me for them, esp. if Glory finally does get better at the non-combat side of things. Gorgon feels like a strange change to me that I'll need to see more to pass judgement on beyond it being in stark contrast to the idea of less culturally linked Tribes. The new glyph isn't bad, but it's also bland and doesn't say anything about the Tribe.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers - Another Tribe that needs a lot more previews on what on Gaia they do with the changes that are being presented to us. I really hope we're not returning to the old &quot;jackal's curse&quot; thing where Rat demands they're all poor, but it feels like treating joining the Tribe more as taking a vow of poverty than actually fighting against the oppression of the exploited classes is where we're headed thanks to that Honor pick. As I noted above, this is the one glyph I actually like.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia - Nothing to really go on yet. One of the Tribes is a pointlessly altered glyph but at least no one that causes oddities. I don't have a problem with them being Wisdom over Honor in theory, but it feels like what the Renown traits actually mean has changed enough that we'll have to see.<br /> <br /> Fianna - Definitely wrong to keep the name. The glyph change is minor but bothers me because it adds a bunch of odd fine detail work to make, and it added a spiral of all things to it.<br /> <br /> Galestalkers - Bad in the unavoidable comparison to Older Brother, otherwise one that really adds to the feeling of there are too many Tribes. The glyph doesn't communicate anything useful to me.<br /> <br /> Ghost Council - Similar to the Galestalkers as they obviously only exist to replace Older Brother, but don't really seem to have a meaningful place with that context being removed, and another glyph that doesn't really seem to say anything. Horned Serpent meeting the absolute lowest bar of fixing Younger Brother's poor use of the uktena myth by translating uktena into English so you can't link it to one specific people any more.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers - Echoing the confusion about the Patron change. <br /> <br /> Red Talons - Echoing the issues with justifying why the existing in the new setup and the odd choice of Renown trait. The minor change to the glyph is a great example of dismissing the idea that these are used as active forms of communication: why have two of the claw marks have a break in them, and who would make the motion to cause that?<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords: Hopefully they can explain the glyph. I actually don't mind the idea of Glory here, because again I want to see Glory as boasting and self-aggrandizement that goes into a culture that puts focus on oral history being more prominent. I don't like the presumption that leadership = honor... politicians struggle with being honorable people.<br /> <br /> Silent Striders: Another Tribe that seems like it wouldn't be here if not for legacy reasons. I don't like the glyph as being overly complex for a Tribe that still focuses on a lot of movement and travel. It's really complex if you think about trying to sit there are draw it with claws.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs: Glyph is the only thing to have a real thought about. The &quot;it's a crown!&quot; thing feels too on the nose, and it runs afoul of the idea that the Tribes aren't linked to cultures because crowns as marks of leadership isn't a universal thing in that sense. It's busy and complicated, and lacks the laconic nature of the old &quot;we're in charge because we're powerful,&quot; one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T15:40:28-07:00","id":1494991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1494989#post1494989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always wondered by the Bone Gnawers couldn't be rich and HAD to be poor. Was it meant to be a Ban from their Totem? I never saw that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revised made this a supernatural issue in their Tribebook where Gnawers just... magically can't keep money. However much they earn, they'll end up wasting it and thus never be able to accumulate wealth.<br /> <br /> W20 actually got rid of that and Gnawers can be as rich as anyone else, it's just less common (represented by not being able to spend base Background points on Resources, just freebies or earning it in play).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T16:03:19-07:00","id":1494993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1494989#post1494989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always wondered by the Bone Gnawers couldn't be rich and HAD to be poor. Was it meant to be a Ban from their Totem? I never saw that.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Heavy Arms said, plus the assumption that lower status in the supernatural community=lower status in human society. Not to mention, books before W20 constantly emphasise that the Gnawers are losers and dregs that are basically incapable of being anything but what they are. Aside from the supernatural compulsion to spend, the underlying assumption is that the Gnawers all come from poverty and poor education, to begin with, and so cannot manage money at all. Apparently, in WoD no college student ever becomes homeless or the assumption is that anyone with higher education becomes a Glass Walker.<br /> <br /> W20 did away with most of that, making the poverty more of a choice to move in areas no one else would.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T17:38:36-07:00","id":1494997,"title":"","content":"The Red Talons seem to be the tribe of trying very hard to instill the Wyld back into humans; I suppose that might fit for certain values of &quot;Purge&quot;. Also, regarding the glyph, the breaks would probably occur naturally; claws aren't knives and don't cut uniformly, which you can see in a lot of scratch and slash wounds. This is particularly true of wolf claws, which tend to be rather blunt compared to cat claws or raptorial talons. Obviously, Crinos and Hispo are exceptions that prove the rule.<br /> <br /> Why bother having Get of Fenris if you have Galestalkers, and tribes aren't bound to cultures? Or should I even ask, given that the Fianna managed to get their foot into the door?<br /> <br /> On that note, I hope that the Silver Fangs stop hyping Russia as their homeland. There have been a bunch of houses spread across Eurasia since 2e, let the fucking Romanov corpses go already. Admittedly, not the kind of information that we got in the post, but it's grating enough that I feel I need to voice it. Loudly, and with much profanity.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T19:03:13-07:00","id":1494998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1494991#post1494991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Revised made this a supernatural issue in their Tribebook where Gnawers just... magically can't keep money. However much they earn, they'll end up wasting it and thus never be able to accumulate wealth.<br /> <br /> W20 actually got rid of that and Gnawers can be as rich as anyone else, it's just less common (represented by not being able to spend base Background points on Resources, just freebies or earning it in play).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, an oath of poverty isn't anything weird in a shamanistic religious society. It's just weird if it WASN'T an oath of poverty.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T19:44:47-07:00","id":1494999,"title":"","content":"It doesn't really make sense, even with what we know of W5, for the Tribes to universally undergo such. They're too diverse.<br /> <br /> The fact that WtA doesn't have ritualistic incorporation of taboos into daily life as a way to demonstrate devotion to a spirit is weird, but should really be a more general issue rather than one for a specific Tribe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T19:56:36-07:00","id":1495001,"title":"","content":"Off hand, I would swap the Children of Gaia, Shadowlords and the Bone Gnawers around.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia become an Honor Tribe - they're one of the leadership tribes. Shadowlords become a Wisdom Tribe - their Wisdom is of the &quot;understand the enemy in order to defeat it&quot; and they tend to know a lot of dark secrets about Wyrm and are more likely to fall than other tribes (there might be a bit of overlap between them and the Ghost Council in that case? But I think it would be manageable). Then the Bone Gnawers become Glory.<br /> <br /> This also means that the two Urban tribes (The Glasswalkers and Bone Gnawers) are Wisdom/Glory. There's no urban focused Honor tribe, which I think makes a meta statement that there's less Honor to be had living in Weaver cities and cutting yourself off from Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-14-2022, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-14T22:07:32-07:00","id":1495003,"title":"","content":"I think we need to be prepared for a significant shift in what the three Renown traits really mean in W5.<br /> <br /> Sure, based on H5, we might just see some things stated and not line up at all with the mechanics, but if Renown is being handled significantly differently, what sorts of actions and lifestyles to associate with each of them is likely to change to.<br /> <br /> The current selections can be made consistent in application for the most part... if you accept Justin's comments about things being changed and apply that to what exactly each represents.<br /> <br /> For example, if we see a Tribe linked with Honor as an indication of a steadfast adherence to a duty or code of conduct in its membership over other considerations, it makes more sense why those four Tribes are the ones that have it compared to the more personal Honor of the older editions. If the new version of Honor focuses on accepting less ideal lifestyles because it's for the good of the many, the Gnawers are honorable for watching the places none of the others will, the Galestalkers and Red Talons are honorable for living off the grid to protect places without adopting tools that might defile them in the long run, and the Silver Fangs get to play on the One Great Man tropes where at personal sacrifice they accept the duty to make the hard call so nobody else has to suffer for that decision. All of that is a conceivably coherent take on Honor, even if a very different one from older WtA.<br /> <br /> There's also a design level thing I can respect that if the Children of Gaia, Shadow Lords and Silver Fangs are the &quot;leadership&quot; Tribes, that each having a different Renown help differentiate their different approaches to leading: The Coggies want to lead through intellect and thoughtful decision making (Wisdom), the ShLs want to lead by crafting a narrative that makes them the best choice (Glory), and the Silver Fangs want to lead because of a sense of duty to endure the weight of the crown (Honor). If they're all Honor, it's less appealing in a few ways.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T02:23:55-07:00","id":1495007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1494986#post1494986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/werewolf-the-apocalypse-tribes-and-renown\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news...bes-and-renown</a> Here</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah that's... decisively underwhelming<br /> <br /> It feels incredibly lazy/silly that tribes are now perfectly analogues as clans. Clans are a way to divide labour among a complex society that needs experts in specific rolls. Werewolves... don't need such complexity and have Auspices for the divisions they do need. Infact for werewolves the simpler things are, the better things are. Having a multi-clan city fullfills necessary functions. Having a multi-tribe sept isn't something essentially beneficial for Garou they just do it because tribal warfare is too costly in modern times. A Ventrue and Nosferatu have a lot to offer one another but a Shadow Lord Galiard and a Children of Gaia galiard fulfil almost precisely the same role and there's not much benefit to having them both over two of one tribe. Tribes were meant to be self-sufficient. <br /> It also makes no political sense for tribes to give their children an even choice of what tribe they'll join. It's in the best interest of a tribe to encourage their children to remain within the tribe they were born to. A Shadow Lord's pup joining the Children of Gaia is a loss for the SL, an embarrasment for the tribe and the totem they follow. Hence, of-fucking-course tribes are going to be geography based rather than whatever the child choses to be. The World of Darkness can't be so idealistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T04:15:30-07:00","id":1495009,"title":"","content":"According to Justin, the process of Tribe selection - in character - is going to be much more personal and spiritual. There's nothing the Garou in W5 can do about their children seeking to join a different Tribe, since it seems like the whole concept of familial heritage and induction via rites of passage are out. After the First Change, new cubs are going to be spiritually drawn to Patrons that fit their true selves. Their parents, and the extant members of the other Tribes, basically don't get a say if the cub and the Patron spirit agree that the cub belongs in that spirit's Tribe.<br /> <br /> The W5 Tribes are going to have to put a lot more work into how they raise their children if they hope to mold them into future members of the same Tribe, and it looks like Tribal cultures will be rewritten to have an &quot;adoption&quot; focused mindset where they take in Garou that aren't of their blood but are of the same &quot;spirit&quot; as the default way of gaining new members.<br /> <br /> While this certainly sounds idealistic from the sense of the Garou getting to be parts of their found families that fit them the best, it's very much not ideal for the Tribes themselves since they become much more dependent on factors outside of their control for new members. Hopefully W5 does something with this new tension they're adding to the game... but I'm not holding my breath for it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T05:10:09-07:00","id":1495013,"title":"","content":"I want to go deeper into why I think Red Talon should have been cut because I love the tribe and do want them to get a fair shake.<br /> <br /> For one, the player response to Talons has been rather meh over the years. The person who made the TV Tropes page for WtA outright states only psychopaths would play them and a Talon in a game would make other players uncomfortable. While I do not think a Talon would make others uncomfortable, I think they are a tribe often played in a way that stalls the story for everyone else. In online games, a Talon cliath throwing a hissy fit at a Glass Walker elder used to be common.<br /> <br /> Getting to play a Red Talon is akin to pulling teeth and for a good reason.<br /> <br /> Second, even in the source material the Talons rarely if ever speak for themselves or are a factor. The revised tribebook's culture chapter is told from the POV of a Shadow Lord and not a Talon. Most often, Talons are mentioned in passing when discussing human eating being forbidden and how the lupus are dying out. The general mood I get from most Talon content is that they are alien and they have all but given up on the Nation.<br /> <br /> Which does not a good Player Character splat make. Every tribe needs some research, but the Talon need you to basically do in-depth research on grey wolves (and then have to accept that the canon for Talons STILL lives by the Alpha/Omega dynamic) and basically play a character that is mostly ignorant and mostly unwilling to change their viewpoints.<br /> <br /> Even if the Shadow Lords and Red Talons are treated as the darkest tribes, the fact is you can speak to a Shadow Lord. You can't to a Talon.<br /> <br /> The way I have made the Talons work for me is by treating their want to be true wolves as something very human. The Talons are defining what a 'wolf' is, while both lupus and regular wolves often fail to match that ideal. They still have writing, rites and general tribal culture, so they are hypocrites in my House Rules.<br /> <br /> But those are my House Rules, not the canon.<br /> <br /> Red Talons are a tribe that is antithetical to the 'everyone can be everything' ethos of W5, their very tribal concept is isolation. Predator Kings in Forsaken are based on Talons and they too are hidebound and refuse to see things differently.<br /> <br /> To me, in order to make the Talons accept everyone, much of the tribe has to be scrapped. While W5 is a reimagining, holding onto the tribal name and totem makes clear connections to their old version. So if the tribe is nothing like the Talons, the references are essentially misleading.<br /> <br /> Besides, you could slot the White Howlers into the tribal list and they would work better than the Talons.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T06:59:43-07:00","id":1495015,"title":"","content":"As mainly <b>Forsaken</b> ST and players of few games in <b>WtA </b>- I wonder - if <b>W5</b> is taking 'adaption take' on joining tribe from <b>WtF</b> - why they do not taken also idea of 5 Renowns? \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> It would make much easier diversify 10-11 tribes over them - it's only 2 Tribes over one Renown - and you can also transplant 5 Renowns to 5 Auspices. But maybe game W5 then too look a like as <b>Forsaken</b>? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-15-2022, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T11:19:31-07:00","id":1495023,"title":"","content":"Nobody has really been able to speculate a good answer to that (I proposed the same idea in another thread, as there are at least three non-playable Tribes in the setting as well to assign Renown too, if not more if the Lost Tribes make it in some fashion and get a Renown assignment).<br /> <br /> Since nobody can puzzle out a holistic design philosophy behind what's being kept, what's being cut, and what's being altered, everyone is left worried that there simply isn't a consistent reasoning and it's going to bleed into the game in a bad way.<br /> <br /> Like... if they wanted to just completely change up the Tribes, without tossing continuity out completely, they could have followed V5 and used the metaplot to completely reorganize the setting. They have almost twenty years of metaplot to fill in with whatever they want. The battles at the end of Revised could have resulted in massive spiritual disruption, causing all the old Tribes to shatter, and new Tribes forming under new conditions. That's basically carte blanche to do whatever you want with the new Tribal setup, and is a clean break that doesn't just toss the past continuity into the bin. Heck it can be used to go way beyond the Tribes, but that's also getting away from the point of the thread.<br /> <br /> You could even work in the Get and Stargazers leaving under a much more relatable and simple reason: they don't want to give up on who they were in the light of a new reality that demands change and adaptation.<br /> <br /> But for now, we also know exceedingly little despite what we do know having such large implications. W5 could nail the landing when the whole book is out for people to read, or fall on it's head. We're not close to knowing for certain, we're just looking at V5 and H5 and the scant previews/Tweets we have. The positive hype is minimal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T11:25:05-07:00","id":1495024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495007#post1495007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah that's... decisively underwhelming<br /> <br /> It feels incredibly lazy/silly that tribes are now perfectly analogues as clans. Clans are a way to divide labour among a complex society that needs experts in specific rolls. Werewolves... don't need such complexity and have Auspices for the divisions they do need. Infact for werewolves the simpler things are, the better things are. Having a multi-clan city fullfills necessary functions. Having a multi-tribe sept isn't something essentially beneficial for Garou they just do it because tribal warfare is too costly in modern times. A Ventrue and Nosferatu have a lot to offer one another but a Shadow Lord Galiard and a Children of Gaia galiard fulfil almost precisely the same role and there's not much benefit to having them both over two of one tribe. Tribes were meant to be self-sufficient.<br /> It also makes no political sense for tribes to give their children an even choice of what tribe they'll join. It's in the best interest of a tribe to encourage their children to remain within the tribe they were born to. A Shadow Lord's pup joining the Children of Gaia is a loss for the SL, an embarrasment for the tribe and the totem they follow. Hence, of-fucking-course tribes are going to be geography based rather than whatever the child choses to be. The World of Darkness can't be so idealistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, people could leave and join other tribes even in 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> One of the Storyteller Screen stories was a Lupus Wendigo who joined the Glass Walkers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T11:33:24-07:00","id":1495025,"title":"","content":"Yeah, honestly 5 Renown types divided among 10 tribes just makes more sense in my eyes. You could also maybe have a tribe depicting a &quot;light&quot; version of a Renown, and another depicting a &quot;dark&quot; version, though obviously that's not strictly necessary. As I see it:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Tribe</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Renown</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Black Furies</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Purity (Dark?)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Bone Gnawers</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Cunning (Light?)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Children of Gaia</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Honor (Light?)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Fianna</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Glory (Light)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Glass Walkers</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Wisdom (Light?)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Galestalkers</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Glory (Dark)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Ghost Council</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Wisdom (Dark?)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Shadow Lords</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Cunning (Dark?)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Silent Striders</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Honor (Dark?)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Silver Fangs</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Purity (Light?)</td> </tr> </table></div> Obviously, I'm not too sure about the Silent Striders here, or the Galestalkers. I took out the Red Talons in addition to the Get and Stargazers, not necessarily that they've fallen to the Wyrm, but it's pretty easy to imagine that they might think that all of the other tribes have become too &quot;humanized&quot; and just leave the Garou Nation to go do their own thing. Overall though, its pretty easy to divide up the Tribes within Forsaken's Renown system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T11:56:19-07:00","id":1495026,"title":"","content":"Dark and light seems a bit constraining and loaded here. Try waxing vs. waning like some of the older books did with Auspices as the Garou associated waxing/waning periods of the moon to impact how Garou would approach their Auspice duties in a similar fashion to what you seem to be going for. Waxing is associated with being direct, straightforward, and aggressive, while waning is associated with being more lateral, thoughtful, and moderated (Waxing = getting close to the full moon and the height of Rage, with waning = getting to the new moon and the minimum of Rage).<br /> <br /> It might move thing around a bit though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T11:58:06-07:00","id":1495027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495023#post1495023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody has really been able to speculate a good answer to that (I proposed the same idea in another thread, as there are at least three non-playable Tribes in the setting as well to assign Renown too, if not more if the Lost Tribes make it in some fashion and get a Renown assignment).<br /> <br /> Since nobody can puzzle out a holistic design philosophy behind what's being kept, what's being cut, and what's being altered, everyone is left worried that there simply isn't a consistent reasoning and it's going to bleed into the game in a bad way.<br /> <br /> Like... if they wanted to just completely change up the Tribes, without tossing continuity out completely, they could have followed V5 and used the metaplot to completely reorganize the setting. They have almost twenty years of metaplot to fill in with whatever they want. The battles at the end of Revised could have resulted in massive spiritual disruption, causing all the old Tribes to shatter, and new Tribes forming under new conditions. That's basically carte blanche to do whatever you want with the new Tribal setup, and is a clean break that doesn't just toss the past continuity into the bin. Heck it can be used to go way beyond the Tribes, but that's also getting away from the point of the thread.<br /> <br /> You could even work in the Get and Stargazers leaving under a much more relatable and simple reason: they don't want to give up on who they were in the light of a new reality that demands change and adaptation.<br /> <br /> But for now, we also know exceedingly little despite what we do know having such large implications. W5 could nail the landing when the whole book is out for people to read, or fall on it's head. We're not close to knowing for certain, we're just looking at V5 and H5 and the scant previews/Tweets we have. The positive hype is minimal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the issue is that there are two design-goals running into opposite directions. On one hand you have W5 as a continuation of V5. That means all the Clans/Tribes are there, some renamed, some changed but the metaplot of old still matters for the most part. BUT... on the other hand, you have Justin Achilli who gives zero shits about the old lore and setting. So we have all these references to old WtA but Justin Achilli will cut out as much of the old lore as possible because he would rather do something more along the lines of CofD. We'll see if Justin Achilli manages to balance this or if this will turn W5 into a mess.<br /> <br /> In regards to the Tribes, when Outstar and Justin Achilli talked about the Creeds in H5, they talked about how it promotes freedom for players. And how that was done, they said is that, for example, the Faithful Creed never specifies what that hunter's faith actually is. Maybe it's a religion but maybe it's science or some virtue or some other kind of ideal. Faithful just means believing in something strongly and it's great how it's all up to the player to interpret what his Faithful hunter-player-character believes in. And I could picture that all the Tribes will be these very broad descriptions where it's left to the players to come up with the specifics of what it really means to be a member of a Tribe. The Tribe isn't supposed to limit any choices in how to portray a member of the Tribe. And that's done by going very broad and vague with the portrayal of the Tribes. I think that's what we'll ultimately get. There will be references to what these Tribes were in old WtA but the goal will be to tell players as little as possible about how to play the Tribes (because that part is supposed to be up to the players).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T12:07:53-07:00","id":1495028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495027#post1495027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the issue is that there are two design-goals running into opposite directions. On one hand you have W5 as a continuation of V5. That means all the Clans/Tribes are there, some renamed, some changed but the metaplot of old still matters for the most part. BUT... on the other hand, you have Justin Achilli who gives zero shits about the old lore and setting. So we have all these references to old WtA but Justin Achilli will cut out as much of the old lore as possible because he would rather do something more along the lines of CofD. We'll see if Justin Achilli manages to balance this or if this will turn W5 into a mess.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Seems weird to bring back the guy who created the original to cut large amounts of the past.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T12:25:43-07:00","id":1495030,"title":"","content":"Justin... didn't create the original (Justin didn't start working at WW until 2e), had public disagreements with Ethan Skemp over WtA not being more like VtM and Mage in Revised to cut back on the 2e gonzoness, and was only in the early planning/design stages of Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T13:32:27-07:00","id":1495038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495028#post1495028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems weird to bring back the guy who created the original to cut large amounts of the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>? <br /> <br /> Yeah....nah. Justin's main contributions to WtA are a couple of essays mostly about embracing the splatterpunk and edgelord elements, some minor rules contributions and a plethora of disparaging or ' just kidding' comments on the old WW forums and news groups. <br /> <br /> Bill Bridges is the OG, who made a great game but also saddled WtA with a bunch of pizza-cutter elements that Ethan Skemp spent the majority of his 2nd and Revised tenure as Developer trying to polish/fix without making the massive metaplot shifts that VtM did every second book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 10-15-2022, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T16:22:06-07:00","id":1495042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495038#post1495038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ?<br /> <br /> Yeah....nah. Justin's main contributions to WtA are a couple of essays mostly about embracing the splatterpunk and edgelord elements, some minor rules contributions and a plethora of disparaging or ' just kidding' comments on the old WW forums and news groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>He was also the dev of Rage before it died the death of most card games in the 90s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T23:42:49-07:00","id":1495050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495024#post1495024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, people could leave and join other tribes even in 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> One of the Storyteller Screen stories was a Lupus Wendigo who joined the Glass Walkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could but it was a massive loss and very few Garou actually went through with it. Your rank gets set to 1, and the social fallout of the act is up to storyteller's discretion (it'd largely depend on the tribe) <br /> <br /> Being so fluid with this thing just undermines the part where Garou are monsters literally driven by rage. Werewolves aren't known for peace and love, they're known for Rip and Tear, and this live and let live attitude is unbecoming of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-15T23:55:01-07:00","id":1495051,"title":"","content":"Even Rage was something Justin took over rather than was the original creator of.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's not a bad thing to be a person who's skills in game dev are in polishing up other people's work. Justin's work on the WoD helped it say strong and grow until market forces nobody could stop came in and messed the TT RPG world as a whole up.<br /> <br /> To get back to the main topic with this, I think the question is... if Justin's skills are best when paired with someone else's first draft as it were... is part of the problem with the Tribes that Justin's basically doing W5 without one? It would explain a lot of his comments and decision making that he knows what's broken, has ideas of how to fix them, but if he usually isn't he one that brings the initial creative framework to the table, he's struggling a bit without the normal constraints he's worked under in the past.<br /> <br /> It feels kinda like the Tribes are so... iffy... in how they've been presented so far because Justin's pitching ways to make them better to himself instead of someone else that's looking to have him make the final version even better.<br /> <br /> It kinda reminds me of what happened with Exalted 3e's development cycle; esp. with how the 3e team was so heavily populated by mid-to-late 2e folks that spent years cleaning up 2e for other people, that when they were suddenly in charge of Exalted themselves, they got off the rails a bit without someone above them saying no or picking between different option they came up with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T00:54:35-07:00","id":1495053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495050#post1495050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being so fluid with this thing just undermines the part where Garou are monsters literally driven by rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>It undermines the value of using the old Tribes so directly for the new edition; all while saying they're changing enough to not consider it a direct continuation anyway.<br /> <br /> Forsaken uses a similar approach to Tribes without undermining the part where werewolves are rage-monsters. If anything, if you're trying to organize creatures known for being rage-monsters into larger scale social units, it makes way more sense to let them join what feels right to them. Trying to force them into groups they might not really care about on a personal and spiritual level is just adding another source of anger, frustration, and tension that'll lead up to Rage fueled blowouts.<br /> <br /> It makes the characters idiots if they think that forcing the Garou to live in family focused units is going to cause less and less severe Rage based domestic violence, than if Garou are expected to be in social groups with less innate social stressors. The Garou don't want Garou murdering each other and kinfolk. Having blood-families be the default situation until their old enough to join a pack, and still giving them pressure to join their birth Tribe, is being really stupid about how Frenzies are known to work in-character.<br /> <br /> In a normal human family, parents telling their teen aged children that they're going to join the family business just like their parents did, and their grandparents did, and so on, is a recipe for shouting, saying things that are hard to take back, and slamming doors. With the Garou it's a good way to have family dinner ruined by fangs, fur, blood, and death.<br /> <br /> Taking cubs away from their families makes the most sense if you care about teaching them to get the basics of controlling their Rage down first and foremost, so they can even make it to joining a Tribe proper.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T01:28:32-07:00","id":1495055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495053#post1495053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In a normal human family, parents telling their teen aged children that they're going to join the family business just like their parents did, and their grandparents did, and so on, is a recipe for shouting, saying things that are hard to take back, and slamming doors. With the Garou it's a good way to have family dinner ruined by fangs, fur, blood, and death.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well this is a load. <br /> For starters, for 98% of recorded human history this is exactly how humans worked. Your dad's a tailor? Congrats, you've got a great opportunity to learn to be a tailor. You could not be a tailor, but that's going to be significantly more difficult than being a tailor. So best be a tailor. If you're the sixth son and nobody looks to be dying anytime soon maybe your mother can pull some strings and get you into masonry, because the mason never had sons, and maybe has a few daughters left around... but anything else? You're going to be at a disadvantage. In times of scarcity &quot;follow your passion&quot; is fucking stupid advice. You follow what's best for you. tradesmen were a minority that had more choice than most. Farmers usually had none (also: I talk with a lot of Indians as part of my job. The steryeotypes are real: if you're talking to an engineer, her mother and father will also be engineers 90% of the time. The one person I met that didn't meet the trend described the drama that occured, but most are just happy to be engineers) <br /> <br /> More pressingly... your tribe wasn't your fucking job. your auspice was your job. Tribe was more like your nationality. If your parents are both french are you going to scream and rant and rave at having to be a frenchman? Are you going to go through a five year immigration process just because you don't like to be texpectedly french as parents? Of fucking course not. So why would a child raised by Shadow Lords rail against being a shadow lord for the sake of not wanting to be told what to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T01:59:11-07:00","id":1495058,"title":"","content":"Aside from the question of how Garou are raised and what their relationship is with their family, isn't the more disruptive idea in the blog that rather than upbringing and legacy, it's the Patron Spirits who decide who gets to be in the Tribe? What the blog suggests as an option is that after the First Change some sort of Harry-Potter-Sorting-Hat is figuratively put on the Garou and he's then told what Tribe he belongs to (based on individual attributes). So in that version, the child of a Shadow Lord parent could become a Silver Fang or Ghost Council member, for example. Basically there's a limited influence of upbringing and legacy in this version because individual qualities could trump both in the question of what Tribe a Garou belongs to.<br /> <br /> And the blog really puts the emphasis on that version because it says: &quot;Some werewolves choose their tribe; <b>many </b>werewolves feel that, somehow, their tribe chooses them.&quot; (Emphasis added by me)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T02:34:33-07:00","id":1495059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495055#post1495055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For starters, for 98% of recorded human history this is exactly how humans worked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not even going to get into a big thing about how historically inaccurate you're being because it doesn't actually matter.<br /> <br /> For the vast majority of human history, humans got stuck with jobs because they didn't have a choice. Sure. That doesn't mean they liked it, and it doesn't mean they were ignorant of the idea that there were other ways to live.<br /> <br /> That's the important part. Humans aren't rage-monsters. They can accept that lot in life and move on, because what else are they going to do? The Garou are rage-monsters. The build up of frustration and resentment when they're told they have to be something they don't want to be (esp. if never even given the chance to try other thing out) builds up Rage, leading to Frenzies and death of loved ones. In the old lore of the game, the vast majority of Garou have Rage-killed a loved one (generally during their First Change). That's normal for them (and not really examined as a reason why the Garou are as messed up as they are when you consider how many of them have untreated mental illness from that). And the only real reason that it's that bad is because the Garou lifestyle maximizes the risks of it rather than doing everything possible to minimize it. It doesn't have to be that way, the Garou created their society that way and decided to keep to those Traditions despite thousands of years of watching other options come and go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tribe was more like your nationality. </div> </div> </div>The problem is that Tribal status for the Garou is never guaranteed. They don't have birthright citizenship. It doesn't matter how much your Shadow Lord parents want you to be a Shadow Lord and how much you want to do it, if you fail your test and now have to hope one of the less strict Tribes will take you in so you don't become a Ronin.<br /> <br /> What W5 is really changing here, is that the tests are done solely by the spirits. The Garou can't try to put their thumbs on the scales by giving favored scions of their lineage cake-walk trials. If you're going to follow Thunder, you have to get Thunder's approval and Thunder's approval alone. And, again, if you're talking about a society built to keep Rage in check, this is clearly a better method because it takes away sources of tension and stress. If the choice is out of individual hands, then they don't build up the expectations that they can influence the results, and then don't have to deal with what happens if the results they want aren't going along smoothly (and, yet again, &quot;drama&quot; here means Frenzies and death and shouting and shame and trying to get people back in line with family expectations).<br /> <br /> It's also rather notable how you're completely flipping the historical argument around as it suits you. The concept of nationality you're using in extremely modern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T02:35:37-07:00","id":1495060,"title":"","content":"I've noticed that tribe in w5 seems to more or less how you 'choose' your tradition in mage. Prior to this in vampire you were chosen, werewolf you where born into it and mage you chose. It was a pretty interesting dynamic with meaningful ramifications I wonder what implications this has for m5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T02:57:03-07:00","id":1495061,"title":"","content":"As old <b>Forsaken</b> ST, I can say - you STILL can have familiar werewolf 'dynasties', even if Totem is choosing it's cubs. Once you have old Shadow Lord family traditions, most of new werewolves in family will surely been raised to become new Shadow Lords, just by knowing what Totem want from new members of the Tribe. It's just less deterministic than 'you were born Shadow Lord, you will die Shadow Lord'. Your upbringing is also taken in consideration in that model. Still, most of families will rise new Shadow Lords, like 90% of time. ( From <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b> game settings observations and how it plays there. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-16-2022, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T02:58:17-07:00","id":1495062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495060#post1495060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've noticed that tribe in w5 seems to more or less how you 'choose' your tradition in mage. Prior to this in vampire you were chosen, werewolf you where born into it and mage you chose. It was a pretty interesting dynamic with meaningful ramifications I wonder what implications this has for m5.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think that's drawing a brighter line between WtA and Mage than really existed. As I pointed out about, Garou aren't born into a Tribe. They were born to a Tribe they may or may not end up in. Garou society puts up a lot of barriers to stigmatize choosing for yourself, but there's always been more to it than birth alone. Mage has likewise always assumed that upbringing and prior belief structures were going to heavily influence Tradition. Beyond just your human upbringing, Mage also included multiple ways your Tradition could be something you were effectively born into. The Himalayan Wars were so bad because both sides believed in reincarnation, and generations of local mages Awakened as reincarnations of previous participants in the wars and got shoved right back into the conflict. It was so bad that even in the modern day some Akashayana and Chakravanti still get saddled with Avatars that force them into their respective Tradition and try to pick fights with enemies from a set of Wars that have been over for over two thousand years.<br /> <br /> Neither game was cut and dry about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T03:06:38-07:00","id":1495064,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but Forsaken has only five Tribes in consideration for that. With W5 it's 11. That would necessarily mean what the Patron Spirits are looking for in an individual Garou has to be more specific in order to distinguish between the Tribes. And that specificity would increase the chances of upbringing and legacy not being enough in producing a Garou with the specific qualities to be a certain Tribe-member.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T03:17:59-07:00","id":1495065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495062#post1495062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I think that's drawing a brighter line between WtA and Mage than really existed. As I pointed out about, Garou aren't born into a Tribe. They were born to a Tribe they may or may not end up in. Garou society puts up a lot of barriers to stigmatize choosing for yourself, but there's always been more to it than birth alone. Mage has likewise always assumed that upbringing and prior belief structures were going to heavily influence Tradition. Beyond just your human upbringing, Mage also included multiple ways your Tradition could be something you were effectively born into. The Himalayan Wars were so bad because both sides believed in reincarnation, and generations of local mages Awakened as reincarnations of previous participants in the wars and got shoved right back into the conflict. It was so bad that even in the modern day some Akashayana and Chakravanti still get saddled with Avatars that force them into their respective Tradition and try to pick fights with enemies from a set of Wars that have been over for over two thousand years.<br /> <br /> Neither game was cut and dry about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its more of a general trend than an absolute, giovanni and revenant stock tzmisce for example are as much born into it as chosen. By contrast the union grabbing a Wiccan who got lucky with her spells 101ing her into being nwo is 'chosen' rather than chose.<br /> <br /> Nonetheless genrally speaking Mages choose, vampires are chosen, werewolves are born.....genrally. Thinking on it v5 re enforced the chosen aspect of vampires by downplaying clans cultural trends which is an interesting contrast to werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-16-2022, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T04:40:28-07:00","id":1495067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495064#post1495064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but Forsaken has only five Tribes in consideration for that. With W5 it's 11. That would necessarily mean what the Patron Spirits are looking for in an individual Garou has to be more specific in order to distinguish between the Tribes. And that specificity would increase the chances of upbringing and legacy not being enough in producing a Garou with the specific qualities to be a certain Tribe-member.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forsaken also has the Lodges to help here, as they have a much more significant impact on their members than Camps do in WtA (at least the old books). As completely customizable, but linked to the Tribes, they can bridge the space between the very broad Tribes and single spirit associated Packs. Lodges can be used to both add variety so that being in the same Tribe as other members of your family doesn't completely cut you off from individual choices about what that means, or as an enticement to stick close to your family as the only way to access the unique secrets a Lodge offers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495065#post1495065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its more of a general trend than an absolute...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it really holds up as a general trend though. Part of it is that the different games have different numbers of splat to pick from, how they come about in-universe, and what level of mechanic impact they have.<br /> <br /> Vampires have Clans. In theory Sect can be picked by multi-Sect games have never been the default way the game is setup. Yes, that does mean as a generality vampires get chosen by their sires.<br /> <br /> Werewolves have Tribes and Auspices, and had Breeds as meaningful choices pre-W5. Part of the issue here is that because Auspice is absolutely selected at birth for a Garou the game plays up Tribe as being something the Garou have a say in by contrast, and even moreso with Breed being something you couldn't pick either. Tribe was the one thing Garou had a say in on some level, not what was picked for them. The Garou as &quot;born&quot; applies much more strongly to everything but Tribe.<br /> <br /> A mage's Avatar and Essence are beyond their personal choice, but mechanically not really significant in how they differ (though that's Mage's approach to a lot of things). Most mages are equally chosen as they choose, because they learn from mentors (unless they're Orphans/Hollowers aka organized Orphans). You can't just say, &quot;I want to be a Hermetic,&quot; and you get to join, you have to find a Hermetic mentor that thinks you're up to snuff to take you in and teach you their methods. While mages have a lot of reasons in modern nights not to be picky about enthusiastic initiates, most of them are still described as knowing that a mage that's ill suited for their Tradition/Convention/Craft/etc. can cause all sorts of problems. Saying that mages &quot;chose&quot; as a general trend is very much ignoring the explicit (until M5 changes something) fact that their main meaningful splat can absolutely tell them to get lost.<br /> <br /> The comes a point where there's just too many exceptions for something to be a general trend.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T06:27:32-07:00","id":1495068,"title":"","content":"Whether you get the exact totem or not during Rite of Passage is very vague, as some books treat RoP as tribal-specific and some as general. In those general cases, the totem that accepts you can be random.<br /> <br /> As Heavy Arms said, you can very much flunk out of your family tribe. Though the tribe with the most failures is gone, you can still be raised in a Fang household all your life and not get accepted by Falcon. That is actually the reason why Bone Gnawers and Children of Gaia are so numerous, a lot of those garou who failed to get into other tribes join them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T08:24:34-07:00","id":1495073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495067#post1495067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage's Avatar and Essence are beyond their personal choice, but mechanically not really significant in how they differ (though that's Mage's approach to a lot of things). Most mages are equally chosen as they choose, because they learn from mentors (unless they're Orphans/Hollowers aka organized Orphans). You can't just say, &quot;I want to be a Hermetic,&quot; and you get to join, you have to find a Hermetic mentor that thinks you're up to snuff to take you in and teach you their methods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not as apt a comparison, since the Purple Paradigm that looms over Mage practically filters everything through some degree of Hermeticism.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T08:47:52-07:00","id":1495074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495064#post1495064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but Forsaken has only five Tribes in consideration for that. With W5 it's 11. That would necessarily mean what the Patron Spirits are looking for in an individual Garou has to be more specific in order to distinguish between the Tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpicking but in <b>Forsaken</b> you have 8 Tribes - 5 of Forsaken and 3 of Pure. As pointed before, some of 'good guys' in Garou Nation from <b>Apocalypse</b> were made clear 'bad guys' Pure in <b>WtF</b> incarnation ( <b>WtF</b> 2E is more nuanced from this divide ). Red Talons becoming Predatory Kings and Shadow Lords becoming Ivory Claws. if I get lore difference correct. That means we have 11 Tribes in <b>Apocalypse</b> and 8 in <b>Forsaken</b> to compare - and they look more and more similar in that take, with 'doubling of Renowns in Tribes' in new schema - and showing how this all can work with 'adopting cub to the Tribe'.<br /> <br /> I want also mention one thing from <b>Forsaken</b> - we have by the games historical lore, great werewolves wolf-blooded Dynasties, especially in <i><b>Forsaken by Rome</b></i> <b>Dark Era</b> - lead by Iron Masters from Forsaken ( sorta Glass Walkers ) and Ivory Claws from Pure ( sorta Shadow Lords ) Tribes. And characters from those still can choose other Tribe, not the one Dynasty is centered on. But those Dynasties still sustain themselves on whole duration of Ancient Rome. It did not collapsed till the Rome itself. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-16-2022, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T09:29:23-07:00","id":1495075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495074#post1495074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nitpicking but in <b>Forsaken</b> you have 8 Tribes - 5 of Forsaken and 3 of Pure. As pointed before, some of 'good guys' in Garou Nation from <b>Apocalypse</b> were made clear 'bad guys' Pure in <b>WtF</b> incarnation ( <b>WtF</b> 2E is more nuanced from this divide ). Red Talons becoming Predatory Kings and Shadow Lords becoming Ivory Claws. if I get lore difference correct. That means we have 11 Tribes in <b>Apocalypse</b> and 8 in <b>Forsaken</b> to compare - and they look more and more similar in that take, with 'doubling of Renowns in Tribes' in new schema - and showing how this all can work with 'adopting cub to the Tribe'.<br /> <br /> I want also mention one thing from <b>Forsaken</b> - we have by the games historical lore, great werewolves wolf-blooded Dynasties, especially in <i><b>Forsaken by Rome</b></i> <b>Dark Era</b> - lead by Iron Masters from Forsaken ( sorta Glass Walkers ) and Ivory Claws from Pure ( sorta Shadow Lords ) Tribes. And characters from those still can choose other Tribe, not the one Dynasty is centered on. But those Dynasties still sustain themselves on whole duration of Ancient Rome. It did not collapsed till the Rome itself. \ud83d\ude0e</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair's fair. Although... to nitpick back a little... If we count the Pure in WtF, we would also have to count the Get and the BSD in WtA which would mean 13 Tribes in W5 and 8 in WtF <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> <br /> (Also, as an aside, how will &quot;the Tribe chooses you&quot; work with Get and BSD...? Can BSD pop up anywhere depending on how the First Change goes?)<br /> <br /> That little bit of fun aside, I mean, what you describe shows how WtF is an actual re-imagination. The Uratha-Pure-divide is a re-imagination of the Garou-Nation and new takes on Tribes . And Wolf-Blooded are also a great new take on Kinfolk with how they can become part of the Pack.<br /> <br /> Also, what you write also again illustrates that when we talk about CofD- or WOD-games we rarely engage in this purely mechanic view like &quot;Tribes is what you do&quot;. There's worldbuilding involved and these setting-elements serve as inspiration for what to do with these concepts. But with Justin Achilli it's just &quot;Tribe is what you do&quot; and here's my list of verbs for how the re-imagined Tribes work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","user":"Knightingale","date":". 10-16-2022, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T14:44:34-07:00","id":1495085,"title":"","content":"Another slight nitpick is that it's actually 9 people forgot that Bale hounds are a tribe and are sort of more aligned with the bsd then the pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T14:45:18-07:00","id":1495086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495028#post1495028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems weird to bring back the guy who created the original to cut large amounts of the past.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495030#post1495030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Justin... didn't create the original (Justin didn't start working at WW until 2e), had public disagreements with Ethan Skemp over WtA not being more like VtM and Mage in Revised to cut back on the 2e gonzoness, and was only in the early planning/design stages of Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to that he quite actively disliked Werewolf and how it was done, and considering Skemp shepherded the golden age of Werewolf, getting somebody whose main valuation comes from comparing the gameline to Vampire is not something I feel bodes well for the game we liked.<br /> <br /> Justin's contribution was mainly to the body of Vampire, and since he was the Lead for the late 2E and whole of Vampire Revised most of that materials has been produced under him. Whether you like that or not is down to the reader.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-16T15:22:50-07:00","id":1495088,"title":"","content":"So, in regards to Justin Achilli's attitude... He had this interaction with Bryan CP Steele on Twitter recently. Bryan CP Steele is a game-developer/author who worked with Renegade Games recently as a writer for their Power Rangers RPG. This is <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1581436457453252608\" target=\"_blank\">their interaction</a>:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Justin Achilli:<br /> See, now, I\u2019d argue that Werewolf is a game about wrong answers only, but they\u2019re extremely righteously performed.<br /> Bryan CP Steele:<br /> *puts on his gurahl voice*<br /> &quot;Now, pup... that's because you and your friends have been asking the wrong questions. Grab a mug, the good stuff, and I'll tell you a tale...&quot;<br /> Justin:<br /> What\u2019s a gurahl<br /> Bryan:<br /> Just an echo from the past that I hope to get the chance to roar back into existence someday. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> #Werewolf5 #gamedesigner #careergoals </div> </div> </div>Obviously, Justin was joking there not knowing what Gurahl are but it's interesting that Bryan assumes Gurahl are something he wants to &quot;bring back in the future&quot;. Maybe I'm reading too much into this but in the context of all the other reveals so far, I could easily picture that the W5 corebook won't acknowledge the existence of any Fera.<br /> <br /> And with that attitude in mind, I think that further supports the notion that Justin probably was never a huge fan of the old WtA lore.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T03:17:16-07:00","id":1495103,"title":"","content":"For now I really like everything I saw from Patron Spirits to tribes and tribal verbs, also the renown associated to each tribe, to me makes sense and I don't want to see these things changed. Can't wait to create local version of Galestalkers, Ghost Council and Black Furies. Indeed, without the old tribal concepts about legacy and blood, the garou seems to be less ''problematic'' and therefore some pathos is lost, but I honestly always storytelled WtA in a dirty, street, horror way ( I still use the Swords or the terrorist conncetion of the Fianna), it's not difficult to me to create terrific single tribe packs that breed young werewolves in order to prepare them for being chosen by their own tribal totem. Actually, the fact that a Patron Spirit choses you because of your attitude, to me sounds like some packs/tribe, could be even more extreme and hardcore than in revised or 20th, since they will try to push some kind of attitudes in their cubs, in ...interesting ways.<br /> <br /> And even if it will not be canon something like that, anyway I will use this idea for my chronicles.<br /> <br /> Yes I know, many things are extremely different from the other editions, and It's right to be negative or skeptical, bu my thoughts are positive, I like this reboot idea, and I like the fact it cuts many ties with older edition, I prefer two feet outside or inside, than one in an one out.<br /> These are my thoughts, but I still think we have few things to talk about. I understand why by the book Players who loves the general fantasy and more epic vibe of werewolf are worried.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 10-17-2022, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T04:15:59-07:00","id":1495105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495103#post1495103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes I know, many things are extremely different from the other editions, and It's right to be negative or skeptical, bu my thoughts are positive, I like this reboot idea, and I like the fact it cuts many ties with older edition, I prefer two feet outside or inside, than one in an one out.</div> </div> </div> </div>On that part I disagree with you. W5 is the definition of one foot inside and one foot outside. That's the issue at hand here. It doesn't go as far as WtF and it doesn't want to be a continuation. So we get this version of WtA that is full of references to old WtA but with like 70 to 80% of the lore cut out with a forced focus on street-level storytelling.<br /> <br /> &quot;Tribe is what you do&quot; isn't some new, interesting take on how Tribes work. The idea is that a player thinks &quot;I want to play a character that is good at doing x.&quot; and then the Tribe is chosen accordingly. Of course, any esoteric stuff like an all-female Tribe or a Lupus-only Tribe or any Tribe that has prerequisites (or any historical, geographical and (problematically, of course) ethnic ties) complicates this simple conception of what role Tribes play in the character-creation-process so that, I imagine, is why all the deeper stuff (tribal traditions, history and character) gets cut out.<br /> <br /> So rather than coming up with a new conception of Tribes and the Garou-Nation like WtF did or trying to deal with all the history, background-detail, flaws and problems of previous editions, W5's take on Tribes is to streamline them and make them a simple choice and leave it up to the players to figure out the details. But the names of most Tribes are kept because W5 still wants to be called Werewolf: The Apocalypse. That alone prevents the game from really doing something new and different. The take W5 has on certain concepts can't be too different. Sure, Gaia's dead or dying but W5 won't say that it's setting is our world but a thousand times worse because we're in the middle of the apocalypse. It will still be the same old WOD from V5 and H5. What it can do, though, is cut out a lot of the lore and downsize the scope and detail of its worldbuilding. That, it seems, how W5 has decided to differentiate itself from previous WtA editions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T04:38:56-07:00","id":1495106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495105#post1495105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that part I disagree with you. W5 is the definition of one foot inside and one foot outside. That's the issue at hand here. It doesn't go as far as WtF and it doesn't want to be a continuation. So we get this version of WtA that is full of references to old WtA but with like 70 to 80% of the lore cut out with a forced focus on street-level storytelling.<br /> <br /> &quot;Tribe is what you do&quot; isn't some new, interesting take on how Tribes work. The idea is that a player thinks &quot;I want to play a character that is good at doing x.&quot; and then the Tribe is chosen accordingly. Of course, any esoteric stuff like an all-female Tribe or a Lupus-only Tribe or any Tribe that has prerequisites (or any historical, geographical and (problematically, of course) ethnic ties) complicates this simple conception of what role Tribes play in the character-creation-process so that, I imagine, is why all the deeper stuff (tribal traditions, history and character) gets cut out.<br /> <br /> So rather than coming up with a new conception of Tribes and the Garou-Nation like WtF did or trying to deal with all the history, background-detail, flaws and problems of previous editions, W5's take on Tribes is to streamline them and make them a simple choice and leave it up to the players to figure out the details. But the names of most Tribes are kept because W5 still wants to be called Werewolf: The Apocalypse. That alone prevents the game from really doing something new and different. The take W5 has on certain concepts can't be too different. Sure, Gaia's dead or dying but W5 won't say that it's setting is our world but a thousand times worse because we're in the middle of the apocalypse. It will still be the same old WOD from V5 and H5. What it can do, though, is cut out a lot of the lore and downsize the scope and detail of its worldbuilding. That, it seems, how W5 has decided to differentiate itself from previous WtA editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand your point.<br /> The thing is that I like what you don't .<br /> I'm totally ok in using words and references cutting 70% of the old meat , using something very different clearly inspired by the original wta. I'm sick about big epic battles and urban fantasy. I want to see what they are creating and I am ok with artistic freedom of doing whatever they want with their thing. If I will end up not liking it, peace , I've got 4 editions to play.<br /> <br /> It's my personal taste, and I dont care if 99% of old players says that I have shitty taste. Don't want to be rude. Just honest. The thread here is thoughts on tribe, so, I said my point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 10-17-2022, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T04:54:01-07:00","id":1495107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495106#post1495106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand your point.<br /> The thing is that I like what you don't .<br /> I'm totally ok in using words and references cutting 70% of the old meat , using something very different clearly inspired by the original wta. I'm sick about big epic battles and urban fantasy.<br /> It's my personal taste, and I dont care if 99% of old players says that I have shitty taste. Don't want to be rude. Just honest. The thread here is thoughts on tribe, so, I said my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine if you like it. I just wanted to clarify in how I would characterize what W5 is doing. Especially because I do agree with the sentiment in your previous post that you prefer something to be either in or out with its choices. Which is why I have a lot more respect for WtF as an exercise in re-imagination compared to what has been shown of W5 so far.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T05:07:28-07:00","id":1495108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495107#post1495107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fine if you like it. I just wanted to clarify in how I would characterize what W5 is doing. Especially because I do agree with the sentiment in your previous post that you prefer something to be either in or out with its choices. Which is why I have a lot more respect for WtF as an exercise in re-imagination compared to what has been shown of W5 so far.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Forsaken is an unique element to me. It's a masterwork from many point of views. It always amaze me how it totally doesn't suffer from the ''spiritual heir'' effect, likle masquerade/requiem and so on. Forsaken is immune from it even from the first edition. In my humble opinion, it's an unique piece that simply can't be copied enough by the new Apocalypse, that's why I'm not worried: forsaken is so different in many different ways from apocalypse, that even if they are going to cannibalize it, it will still be different. <br /> <br /> In all this story, what I am truly worried about, is the fact that Wtf will probably be dead, if their intention is to milk the WoD for years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T05:07:33-07:00","id":1495109,"title":"","content":"Something to think of, this is how one writer for WtF wrote the WtA tribes to Forsaken: <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160429104331/https://www.zeropointinformation.com/blog/2012/thirteen-forsaken-tribes/\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20160429...rsaken-tribes/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T05:14:32-07:00","id":1495110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495109#post1495109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to think of, this is how one writer for WtF wrote the WtA tribes to Forsaken: <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160429104331/https://www.zeropointinformation.com/blog/2012/thirteen-forsaken-tribes/\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20160429...rsaken-tribes/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting I did something really similar time ago.<br /> I think the only difference was strength instead of insight for the Fangs, and Evasion instead of Strength for the Wendigo","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T05:32:11-07:00","id":1495111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495109#post1495109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to think of, this is how one writer for WtF wrote the WtA tribes to Forsaken: <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160429104331/https://www.zeropointinformation.com/blog/2012/thirteen-forsaken-tribes/\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20160429...rsaken-tribes/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I went mostly with <b>WtA</b> Tribes as <b>WtF</b> Lodges - as it has much more sense, with all cultural backdrop of<b> WtA</b> Tribes and various... let's say 'specifics' of Tribes. It makes them great as Lodges in <b>WtF</b> structure. <b>Werewolf Translation Guide</b> also points it. For <b>WtF</b> 2E I made <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867500-apocalypse-tribes-as-2e-lodges?p=867680#post867680\">about half of those Tribes-Lodges already</a>. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-17-2022, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T05:51:52-07:00","id":1495113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495109#post1495109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to think of, this is how one writer for WtF wrote the WtA tribes to Forsaken: <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160429104331/https://www.zeropointinformation.com/blog/2012/thirteen-forsaken-tribes/\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20160429...rsaken-tribes/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's worth noting that Stew Wilson wasn't just one writer for WtF... he worked on almost every WtF1e book, developed WtF2e,and worked on all of W20 as well (he was the dev that nWW/Paradox wouldn't stop meddling with for W20). While Stew had publicly said he was intended to step away from RPG work to focus on other things as W20 was winding down and WtF 2e core was done, the fact that Paradox utterly burned their bridges with him is a downright shame because he stands on par with Ethan Skemp in terms of the people that should be the first choices on who you'd want to be able to consult about W5. It's hard to fathom how much informal advice Justin couldn't get if Stew is still as adamant about not working with Paradox after W20 Changing Ways, considering Stew is the only person to be the lead dev on WtA and WtF at the same time (and there weren't any public signs of difficulty between them like there were with Justin and Ethan).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T06:19:57-07:00","id":1495115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495113#post1495113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's worth noting that Stew Wilson wasn't just one writer for WtF... he worked on almost every WtF1e book, developed WtF2e,and worked on all of W20 as well (he was the dev that nWW/Paradox wouldn't stop meddling with for W20). While Stew had publicly said he was intended to step away from RPG work to focus on other things as W20 was winding down and WtF 2e core was done, the fact that Paradox utterly burned their bridges with him is a downright shame because he stands on par with Ethan Skemp in terms of the people that should be the first choices on who you'd want to be able to consult about W5. It's hard to fathom how much informal advice Justin couldn't get if Stew is still as adamant about not working with Paradox after W20 Changing Ways, considering Stew is the only person to be the lead dev on WtA and WtF at the same time (and there weren't any public signs of difficulty between them like there were with Justin and Ethan).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for adding this, it really does put the conversions in context.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T07:18:56-07:00","id":1495117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Glory</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Honor</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Wisdom</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Wyld</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Black Furies</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">GaleStalkers?</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Children of Gaia</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Weaver</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Finana?</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Bone Gnawer</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Glass Walkers</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Wyrm</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Shadow Lords?</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Red Talons?</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Ghost Council?</td> </tr> </table></div> Here is my quick and dirty thoughts on the tribes (according to the idea about a matching Triant-Renown). Anything with a question mark I'm not sure if that is the best fit. Of course, this is more of a thought experiment rather then something I think was actually part of the design. With that I'm not really sure where to put Silent Striders or Silver Fangs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T08:27:21-07:00","id":1495119,"title":"","content":"&quot;x as verbs&quot; sounds like such a pompous move. Like not only are you reducing complexity and nuance you're also pretending to be an artist while doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T08:36:36-07:00","id":1495120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495117#post1495117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Glory</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Honor</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Wisdom</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Wyld</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Black Furies</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">GaleStalkers?</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Children of Gaia</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Weaver</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Finana?</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Bone Gnawer</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Glass Walkers</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Wyrm</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Shadow Lords?</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Red Talons?</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Ghost Council?</td> </tr> </table></div> Here is my quick and dirty thoughts on the tribes (according to the idea about a matching Triant-Renown). Anything with a question mark I'm not sure if that is the best fit. Of course, this is more of a thought experiment rather then something I think was actually part of the design. With that I'm not really sure where to put Silent Striders or Silver Fangs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the only merit to changing how tribes get renown is if you threw cunning into some tribes. BG replace honour with cunning, SL replace glory. Glass walkers replace wisdom... no... I see problems with that.<br /> <br /> Cunning is great. We should scrap werewolf as the main changing breed and use Ratkin instead. Way more fun. Skaven&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;skinwolves.<br /> (nah for reals ratkin are the best)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T08:44:07-07:00","id":1495121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495119#post1495119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;x as verbs&quot; sounds like such a pompous move. Like not only are you reducing complexity and nuance you're also pretending to be an artist while doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>When Justin Achilli started talking about that, the thing it reminded me of was Monte Cook's Cypher System like with Numenera or Invisible Sun, for example, where you make all these choices during character-creation and at the end, you get a &quot;sentence&quot; describing your character.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T09:37:49-07:00","id":1495124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495120#post1495120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the only merit to changing how tribes get renown is if you threw cunning into some tribes. BG replace honour with cunning, SL replace glory. Glass walkers replace wisdom... no... I see problems with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like if we are here to armchair dev I really don't see a reason why there shouldn't be tons of different renowns for character creation that are not linked to anything. Like I don't see why you couldn't have a 'Glory' Glass walker or an Honor Black Fury. Especially since it seems you are going to get a gift from your tribe, one from your auspice, and one for your renown (at least that is how &quot;Associated Renown helps establish the tribes\u2019 archetypes (in game terms)&quot;) and the following from that article &quot;Garou can definitely earn Renown outside that which is the hallmark of their tribe, allowing players to portray characters \u201cagainst type\u201d if they wish.&quot; Which really makes me wonder why even have that chart at all?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495120#post1495120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cunning is great. We should scrap werewolf as the main changing breed and use Ratkin instead. Way more fun. Skaven&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;skinwolves.<br /> (nah for reals ratkin are the best)</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, I think that this point <i>not</i> including the fera in your base game is going to create eyebrow raises. Like you can make a game that has 3-5 tribes of each fera based on renown or hell have cross Fera Tribes! Like Bone Gnawers are a Garou-Ratkin tribe if anything that would help make some of the overlap of these have uniqueness to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T12:40:03-07:00","id":1495133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495124#post1495124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which really makes me wonder why even have that chart at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>My speculation is that Renown is going to work mostly like Forsaken (but also tied into the WoD5 &quot;risky dice&quot; thing). So you get three starting dots of Renown, one for Tribe, one for Auspice, and one free pick. So it's really just the kind of stuff that would end up on a char-gen summary.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T13:06:02-07:00","id":1495134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495133#post1495133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My speculation is that Renown is going to work mostly like Forsaken (but also tied into the WoD5 &quot;risky dice&quot; thing). So you get three starting dots of Renown, one for Tribe, one for Auspice, and one free pick. So it's really just the kind of stuff that would end up on a char-gen summary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that you point that out, I can see that. So instead of like rage dice (or maybe in addition), have renown dice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T13:32:47-07:00","id":1495137,"title":"","content":"It's hard to guess too well yet, but I'm thinking it could be similar to Desperation and Despair in H5, where Renown takes the Desperation role, and Rage takes the Despair role. This would also follow suit with Forsaken were Rage is a more even complication for all werewolves instead of varying wildly by Auspice/XP choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T17:09:58-07:00","id":1495146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495124#post1495124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, I think that this point <i>not</i> including the fera in your base game is going to create eyebrow raises. Like you can make a game that has 3-5 tribes of each fera based on renown or hell have cross Fera Tribes! Like Bone Gnawers are a Garou-Ratkin tribe if anything that would help make some of the overlap of these have uniqueness to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>When W5 was first announced I was hoping that's where things would go. With Gaia &quot;dying&quot; the Werewolves and Fera would be putting aside some of their differences and you'd see tribes teaming up with groups of Fera more often in general and some tribes getting closer with specific groups of fera like Bone Gnawers and Ratkin. Alas that seems like it's not the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-17T21:43:16-07:00","id":1495151,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I'm too keen on that really; at least not in a game called Werewolf and all. I appreciate how the Fera flush out the setting and allow of lot of play options that are hard to fit the Garou into, but at the same time they massively clutter up the game, frequently cause a lot of mechanical overlaps, and make the setting muddy in detrimental fashion instead of heightening a sense of mystery and unpredictability. <br /> <br /> The more you incorporate the Fera into the default mode of play of WtA, the less a bunch of Garou concepts feel important (and I already see W5 has having too many Tribes as it is on those grounds). If the Ratkin become essentially accepted as full allies of the Garou, the Gnawers tend to get pushed out of the spot light.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T07:32:32-07:00","id":1495163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495151#post1495151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I'm too keen on that really; at least not in a game called Werewolf and all. I appreciate how the Fera flush out the setting and allow of lot of play options that are hard to fit the Garou into, but at the same time they massively clutter up the game, frequently cause a lot of mechanical overlaps, and make the setting muddy in detrimental fashion instead of heightening a sense of mystery and unpredictability.<br /> <br /> The more you incorporate the Fera into the default mode of play of WtA, the less a bunch of Garou concepts feel important (and I already see W5 has having too many Tribes as it is on those grounds). If the Ratkin become essentially accepted as full allies of the Garou, the Gnawers tend to get pushed out of the spot light.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could only ever see them as allies of Bone Gnawers, and only because BGs are on the bottom rung of Garou society. They probably wouldn't want to leap into a system where they're going to get officially shat on even more.<br /> <br /> As for mechanical overlap, if you add in yet more different types of Renown all around, that'll probably make a pretty big difference according to what we've heard about the plans for the edition. Lots of Fera already have markedly different Renown (Ratkin notably so, with Infamy, Obligation, and Cunning), so it's not that big of a leap. Hopefully, W5 doesn't core dump concepts like H5 did, so that the mechanical distinctions can remain/be possible in the first place.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T08:04:45-07:00","id":1495164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495163#post1495163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hopefully, W5 doesn't core dump concepts like H5 did, so that the mechanical distinctions can remain/be possible in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'd be really surprised if we see any Fera in the W5 &quot;reimagining.&quot; They are probably be cut with the idea that they were never there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T09:37:27-07:00","id":1495167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495163#post1495163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could only ever see them as allies of Bone Gnawers, and only because BGs are on the bottom rung of Garou society. They probably wouldn't want to leap into a system where they're going to get officially shat on even more.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's already fairly close to the case of how things were in previous edition, except that even the Ratkin and Gnawers know their alliance works better at a distance. Any change towards closer relationships (which is what I was responding to) would be more integrated than this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for mechanical overlap, if you add in yet more different types of Renown all around, that'll probably make a pretty big difference according to what we've heard about the plans for the edition. </div> </div> </div>The comes a point where too many Renown categories stops making the mechanically significant and instead are just all the same with different flavor that comes down to, &quot;are you following the stereotypes of your splat?&quot;<br /> <br /> That's not necessarily a bad thing if designed right, but making too many options a functional game mechanic tends to mean simplifying them too much that they aren't seen as mechanical distinctions over narrative ones. For example, Nature/Demeanor isn't something people point to as a real mechanical distinction between otherwise similar characters, they just encourage some different character quirks in how to regain WP in characters that might help break up the sameness when RPing, but not really matter during rules-heavy segments of the game like combat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T09:48:13-07:00","id":1495168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495167#post1495167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's already fairly close to the case of how things were in previous edition, except that even the Ratkin and Gnawers know their alliance works better at a distance. Any change towards closer relationships (which is what I was responding to) would be more integrated than this.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully, something that won't get thrown out in W5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The comes a point where too many Renown categories stops making the mechanically significant and instead are just all the same with different flavor that comes down to, &quot;are you following the stereotypes of your splat?&quot;<br /> <br /> That's not necessarily a bad thing if designed right, but making too many options a functional game mechanic tends to mean simplifying them too much that they aren't seen as mechanical distinctions over narrative ones. For example, Nature/Demeanor isn't something people point to as a real mechanical distinction between otherwise similar characters, they just encourage some different character quirks in how to regain WP in characters that might help break up the sameness when RPing, but not really matter during rules-heavy segments of the game like combat. </div> </div> </div>Renown types are far more constrained than Archetype/Demeanor types. The former get set in number in the concept of a character type; the latter proliferated across all types of different books. Presumably, you also just use Renown to highlight what values that a given changer's society values the most. Quite frankly, some Fera are overdue for this; Mokole, for example, used the same Renown types as Garou, but I don't know if the Memory should lean on the same pillars of society that the Talons do. Like, RAW, Mokole also gain Glory for Battle Scars, and that might be a bit <i>counter-productive</i> for their role.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T12:24:51-07:00","id":1495177,"title":"","content":"Have you ever tried to run a WtA game with 4+ Fera types at the same time with the different Renown types? It's a complete pain in the ass. There's a reason Beast Court games override individual Fera Renown systems for one unified one instead.<br /> <br /> That's what I'm talking about. If you keep expanding the types of Renown, and you expect to use all of them at once, it gets unworkable. You end up reducing them in some fashion.<br /> <br /> Even in the existing Fera schemes, you have to treat Duty, Obligation, Honor, and Obedience as distinct things even though... they're very minor and nuanced differences that all revolve around similar broad strokes concepts. It's not bad world building, but it's not great game design because they're not like Nature/Demeanor where it's just flavor on what a person or society values, but ultimately it's a loose guideline on one mechanic's application. They're in-depth and highly relevant systems to a lot of stuff.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T13:06:27-07:00","id":1495181,"title":"","content":"But I agree with MrNatas... I'd be surprised if Fera are a thing that is acknowledged in W5. And isn't that one of the issues with what is shown of W5's approach so far? Renown as a system had its issues but like with so many other things I believe Justin Achilli's solution will be to just remove them from continuity - and that will be it. The new Renown-system (Glory, Wisdom, Honor) works because any complexity is removed. What I imagine one hard line will be is &quot;high Renown=selfish/bad&quot; but other than that acquiring Renown is just a matter of roleplaying-prompts and how those could spice up a W5 session.<br /> <br /> Also, Justin Achilli just <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1582453961474592769\" target=\"_blank\">tweeted</a> that there's gonna be another Dev-blog about W5 this month.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T13:19:24-07:00","id":1495183,"title":"","content":"One thing that makes me ponder, especially given the 'everyone can be in any tribe' nature of the game, is how this will show in practical play and how would it be more functional than the older tribe versions.<br /> <br /> Let us start with Red Talons because a low-hanging fruit is still a fruit. Let us say the Talons keep their anti-civilization and anti-humanity opinions. This will result in them being once again shelved because the average player does not want to go full Luddite. But if we remove their dislike of civilization and humanity, we are left with a tribe that is grumpy and fighty. What makes them stand out from Furies, Gale Stalkers or Fianna?<br /> <br /> How to do the tribe so it keeps its uniqueness, yet be something people want to play?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T13:26:11-07:00","id":1495184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495183#post1495183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that makes me ponder, especially given the 'everyone can be in any tribe' nature of the game, is how this will show in practical play and how would it be more functional than the older tribe versions.<br /> <br /> Let us start with Red Talons because a low-hanging fruit is still a fruit. Let us say the Talons keep their anti-civilization and anti-humanity opinions. This will result in them being once again shelved because the average player does not want to go full Luddite. But if we remove their dislike of civilization and humanity, we are left with a tribe that is grumpy and fighty. What makes them stand out from Furies, Gale Stalkers or Fianna?<br /> <br /> How to do the tribe so it keeps its uniqueness, yet be something people want to play?</div> </div> </div> </div>Give them a technogaian perspective from the gaian half of the concept, bringing the animal/spirit voice to the table of what the collected ecosystem of civilization and wilderness could look like in future?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T13:27:13-07:00","id":1495185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495183#post1495183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that makes me ponder, especially given the 'everyone can be in any tribe' nature of the game, is how this will show in practical play and how would it be more functional than the older tribe versions.<br /> <br /> Let us start with Red Talons because a low-hanging fruit is still a fruit. Let us say the Talons keep their anti-civilization and anti-humanity opinions. This will result in them being once again shelved because the average player does not want to go full Luddite. But if we remove their dislike of civilization and humanity, we are left with a tribe that is grumpy and fighty. What makes them stand out from Furies, Gale Stalkers or Fianna?<br /> <br /> How to do the tribe so it keeps its uniqueness, yet be something people want to play?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, my bet is that characterizations only matter in terms of &quot;Tribe is what you do&quot;, so at most Red Talons just means &quot;You want to play a character that likes to destroy shit like machines and things made by human hand in general...? Well, then Red Talons is your Tribe.&quot;. And that's all there will be to Red Talons. There will be Archetypes alluding to this and maybe a tiny Reference to a lot of Lupus being in this Tribe. But that's it.<br /> <br /> Also in my version of deciphering the verbs, I think the Red Talons are also now the Tribe who protects Wyld-places, Caerns in general and they make sure those remain places only accessed by Garou/Kinfolk. That's how I picture them in W5 going by what has been shown so far.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T16:50:22-07:00","id":1495203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495177#post1495177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever tried to run a WtA game with 4+ Fera types at the same time with the different Renown types? It's a complete pain in the ass. There's a reason Beast Court games override individual Fera Renown systems for one unified one instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still sounds like less of a pain than Exalted 2nd edition. Which is really the lion's share of my ST experience (for almost a year!), so I'm less likely to see that as a deal-breaker, personally. Then, though, I was blessed with players who knew what all their Charms did.<br /> <br /> But if they're going the Forsaken route, Renown might be easier to track in that it is purchased instead of banked up. Not necessarily great, there, if we're going for Apocalypse flavor. Alternately, it might have a simplified track where you just check off a set number of milestones to get a new dot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's what I'm talking about. If you keep expanding the types of Renown, and you expect to use all of them at once, it gets unworkable. You end up reducing them in some fashion.<br /> <br /> Even in the existing Fera schemes, you have to treat Duty, Obligation, Honor, and Obedience as distinct things even though... they're very minor and nuanced differences that all revolve around similar broad strokes concepts. It's not bad world building, but it's not great game design because they're not like Nature/Demeanor where it's just flavor on what a person or society values, but ultimately it's a loose guideline on one mechanic's application. They're in-depth and highly relevant systems to a lot of stuff. </div> </div> </div>That's how things were. W5 will have little of the Was, from what we're being shown. As such, the Renown can be moved further apart, if need be, so that it's not a series of edge cases.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T18:31:22-07:00","id":1495208,"title":"","content":"Well, having played plenty of WtA and Exalted 2e, let me put it in Exalted terms.<br /> <br /> The Garou and Fera are a lot like the different kind of Exalted. They all work on the same basic set of rules, but each have their own set of unique quirks to deal with. While they share more generic Charms than the Exalted do, each group adds their own need Charms to learn/have your players know on top of the innate powers and weaknesses.<br /> <br /> The Renown categories though, are like having each have their own different set of Virtues. Instead of thinking about how a combat might require a Valor roll, it's Valor for one PC, Bravado for another, Glory for yet another, and so on. Even getting past the bean-counting of how the old Renown worked, and moving to something more like how Renown works in Forsaken, juggling a completely different set for multiple PCs is just piling on the ST workload.<br /> <br /> There's a reason Scion dumped that exactly way of doing it where every PC had a pick of Virtues from a big list, making it a chore to judge how each character would react to situations based on that.<br /> <br /> What I've been trying to get at, is that if you add the Fera to the default game, you end up reducing features like custom Renown sets for them, because it's too hard to have as many as there are in WtA now. W5 would be correct to reduce the number of Renown traits even at the cost of how it used to differentiate the Fera.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T19:15:08-07:00","id":1495215,"title":"","content":"Honestly not sure equating renown to virtues is comparable.<br /> <br /> In my experience at least, renown wasn't hard to keep track of because most of the work is on the Player's part to remember and they only need to keep track of their own character. Players are actively Trying to earn renown so their character can advance and renown is only issued for pretty grand and obvious acts on the player's part(putting it in the same ballpark as bonus XP).<br /> <br /> Sticking to the old system also meant player's gravitated toward the mindset of their character. A Nuwisha is going to actively try to be funny and informative because he needs humor and teaching to advance. Anananasi is going to be more withdrawn, thoughtful, and by-the-book because they're graded on their cunning, wisdom, and obedience to the law. Garou are going to be high off their own adrenaline most of the time because two thirds of their renown code is &quot;fight the thing, but look awesome doing it&quot; and &quot;hold up the old ways, which mostly end with: fight the thing in fair combat&quot;. The system encouraged people to actually <b>Role</b>-play rather than just <i>roll</i>-playing the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 10-18-2022, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-18T23:47:03-07:00","id":1495224,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I've run a few games with mixed Fera types and never found it a huge issue since the players were doing a lot of the legwork in keeping track of their renown or suggesting that an action should count or not. It's like in D&amp;D I've rarely run with players that were thoroughly uninterested in keeping track of their exp, or gold or magic items.<br /> <br /> Admittedly if the group didn't care and the ST had to track everything, that would be a mess. But running a group that didn't care or couldn't do something like keep track of their character's renown would be mess anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T01:42:07-07:00","id":1495227,"title":"","content":"I've run some games with mixed fera types (around 100 sessions worth), and usually it was not a big problem to track things, and there were funny situations where a messup caused someone to lose renown while someone else got it. The problem that I've noticed is something else - the system is not set up for a very long campaign, because you can actually crush the Rank limits in a pretty small amount of sessions. And that could lead to someone becoming Rank 4 or 5 in a year or two of gametime which seems... odd?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T01:44:48-07:00","id":1495228,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the players don't say how much any given action is worth. There's the charts in the books (which are supposed to be suggestions, and even then frequently offer up ranges the ST needs to assign).<br /> <br /> When everyone's on the same Renown, you can just say, &quot;that was worth X Glory, Y Honor, Z Wisdom,&quot; and it's as simple as passing out XP, and there might be a few individual modifiers that might come up (even though the books generally recommend that Renown is shared by a group).<br /> <br /> Just having a Garou and a Bastet fight side by side against a squad of fomori means you have to look at the fight from Glory vs. Ferocity (and depending on how it goes it might interact with other Renown traits too). They're no 1:1 charts as each puts slightly different emphasis on different actions. You can easily run into situations where a fight is 5 Glory for the Garou, but 7 Ferocity for the Bastet, after having run through the fight against both charts. Every additional Fera type that uses different Renown means a new chart to run a scene through, and a different set of numbers to give to each player individually.<br /> <br /> None of this matters to the players being good about keeping track of their numbers.<br /> <br /> Also, it feels like we're not talking about the same rules here. The Renown charts are full of things that are not &quot;grand and obvious,&quot; if the books didn't say Garou get 1 temp Honor ever month they perform their regular duties at the Sept... would that be obvious from the general description of Honor? It's certainly not a grand act of Honor.<br /> <br /> Sure if you completely toss the sample charts and eyeball everything it's going to be easier, but that just sounds like what I was already saying: you end up reducing the individuality of each as the similar Renown traits are going to lump together quickly. Without the larger sample award charts you're not going to have the examples of where Glory and Ferocity, or Honor and Duty, diverge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T04:27:37-07:00","id":1495232,"title":"","content":"I don't see your point. Do you actually stop the game when a deed happens to consult the charts and assign renown, how many deeds on average do you have in a session?<br /> <br /> I've always done that at the end of the session, and it would make a cool discussion with everyone as they would discuss the high points of the session and try to angle for another point here or there or bemoan this or that loss. You go through the charts together and it's a part of the experience and totally in tune with the whole &quot;building of your own legend&quot;. After a whlle the charts pretty much become second nature, and you only end up having to check for that irritating Ananasi player who appears every 5th session what exactly Obligation does.The only thing that I would do in the middle of the session is a penalty for something horrible going down, and even that happened rarely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T05:09:04-07:00","id":1495235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495232#post1495232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I've been pretty clear...<br /> <br /> The more Renown traits you add that, the more work you put on the ST because each assignment of Renown has to go through that many more filters.<br /> <br /> This is amplified further as each chart mixes Renown types together so even if PCs share one Renown trait, the final results of their Renown assignments will be skewed by the Renown traits they don't share in common. <br /> <br /> I do not get the push back here. Are any of you actually arguing that the old mutli-Fera Renown each with a unique chart is as easy as one Chart for everyone? Is anyone explicitly saying that adding new charts does not increase the complexity of the game?<br /> <br /> Are you arguing that how people react to system complexity is universal, and that if something comes easily to one person after a bit of play, it will come easily to everyone equally?<br /> <br /> Because if you're not arguing that, what you're saying doesn't make any sense. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you actually stop the game when a deed happens to consult the charts and assign renown, how many deeds on average do you have in a session? </div> </div> </div><br /> In person, I usually do by scene so that sessions with a few scenes don't have things get lost in the shuffle.<br /> <br /> Online, where I can have logs, I'll do it between games because I can actually go back and see what happened rather than trying to do it all by memory or try to add keeping lots of Renown notes to my list of ST duties.<br /> <br /> I fail to see why this matters. It's still more work I had to do when I ran these things in the past than when I run single Renown chart games like straight Garou or Beast Courts.<br /> <br /> I also get the feeling that you all have gotten very lucky with your players. I play with people that have been doing WtA for decades and barely know the Garou chart. They're so used to games where the ST kept tight control over it, they never bothered because the ST just assigned numbers and they moved on, so there was no point to them to learn it. They had a vague idea for a general sense of what's &quot;good&quot; and &quot;bad,&quot; but beyond that they wouldn't have a clue about why one fight got them 4 temp glory and another got them 8 even if the first one felt vaguely more &quot;glorious&quot; in the mind..<br /> <br /> I've also been in games where the ST considered trying to haggle for a bit more here or there behavior worthy of kicking people out of the game because they don't want to have to deal with everyone trying to &quot;game&quot; the system (which you already noted does not need players to try to milk it for Renown even faster than it already goes).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> After a whlle the charts pretty much become second nature, and you only end up having to check for that irritating Ananasi player who appears every 5th session what exactly Obligation does </div> </div> </div>So, basically, you know exactly what I'm talking about, but you got lucky with your group actually being into the Renown charts for the most part,and instead of realizing that for a lot of people that &quot;barely shows up Ananasi player&quot; is probably half the group of otherwise awesome and engaged players you don't want to turn away because those big charts aren't their thing.<br /> <br /> From a game design perspective, making people learn those charts to play a multi-Fera game is not worth the end result of rewarding them for playing in their niches; playing to your niche is basically the whole point of such a setup. The game does not actually need 17 different Renown traits, the vast majority of which could easily be collapsed into 4-7 of them depending on your inclinations, and have everyone just use one standard list that would be bigger to make the Tribal Renown links we're seeing in the preview more sensible, and giving everyone favored Renown traits would let the Fera (even if it's a W5 STV book) express their interests that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T07:19:25-07:00","id":1495242,"title":"","content":"I am not necessarily advocating for the old design as I'm aware it can be a bit cumbersome, my players were interested more in their deeds than the tables. The onus of adjudicating and tracking what the Renown means and how it has been spread has always been on the ST. One could argue that one of the biggest problems of the WoD games was not the metaplot, but the actual amount of setting material that one had to digest and use on a regular basis to run a game as presented.<br /> <br /> However, I do feel that those charts were doing a huge amount of world building - something that was crucial to presenting the values and the way of life of the Garou. The shifters need the rigid and strange rules and behaviors to make their experience unique. Skipping them makes sense in the paradigm of cutting things to simplify and eliminate the setting burdern of a game, but it detracts from the experience as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T08:09:59-07:00","id":1495243,"title":"","content":"I'm just echoing what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> is saying. The bean counting of renown has never been an issue for the games I have been in or run, even the mixed Fera ones. I do, however, agree that from the standpoint of truncating themes in mixed Fera games from only Garou games. I.E. Ratkin would be the &quot;equivalent&quot; to a Bone Gnawer in a mixed Fera game from the standpoint of 'grunge street punk.' I do feel like there is enough difference between Tribes and Fera that you could easily have a Ratkin and Bone Gnawer in the same game and they be different to not have overlap but, I think it becomes more of an economy of races/classes kind of deal. If you are playing a game and have two urban infiltrators, you are going to pick up the &quot;better&quot; one typically. <br /> <br /> Moving back to the Tribes of W5<br /> <br /> Do you guys expect to see Black Spiral Dancers and Get of Fenrir in their own book, in kind of a similar vein to the V5 Sabbat book? I can't imagine that we wouldn't see them ever but, I am curious if there would be even any kind of rules to play either of these in the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T08:55:13-07:00","id":1495247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495243#post1495243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you guys expect to see Black Spiral Dancers and Get of Fenrir in their own book, in kind of a similar vein to the V5 Sabbat book? I can't imagine that we wouldn't see them ever but, I am curious if there would be even any kind of rules to play either of these in the corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will there be books for antagonists in W5, yes. But will there be rules to play those? Considering what has been happening with WOD5E so far, I'm like 99% sure the answer is no. That will be something someone (maybe even one of the writers working on the antagonist-books) will write up and put up on the STV.<br /> <br /> I also saw this on<a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1582736879954563074\" target=\"_blank\"> Justin Achilli's Twitter</a> and thought this is another comment that gives us an insight into what he's thinking:<br /> <br /> Someone asked him about the aesthetics of various movies that would be suitable as inspiration for WOD-games and then Justin said this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was briefly swapped out for the non-focal &quot;neo-noir&quot; approach of V5, but I've been pushing WoD5 back to an updated Gothic-Punk. </div> </div> </div>There are a couple things that come to mind reading this: 1) He wants WOD5E to go in a different direction than V5 2) He thinks V5 was &quot;neo-noir&quot; and how it was applied was &quot;unfocused&quot; 3) His idea of &quot;Gothic Punk&quot; (as portrayed in H5, I guess) is what he'll be going for with future WOD5E-releases.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T10:25:24-07:00","id":1495248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495208#post1495208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, having played plenty of WtA and Exalted 2e, let me put it in Exalted terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even remotely necessary, I am familiar with both. I also know that there are systems that other WoD games used that were like Renown but much simpler, like the Tempers from Land of Eight Million Dreams. That's why I mentioned the alternative setup of just keeping tally marks (in fact, that was how Virtues used to work in Hunter... but that was much more cumbersome due to replacing xp to buy powers). With the tack toward old systems being readily described by Fire Water Burn, there's no reason to assume that it would, especially when the systems are threatening to go on an out of place Forsaken binge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T10:26:25-07:00","id":1495249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495247#post1495247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be books for antagonists in W5, yes. But will there be rules to play those? Considering what has been happening with WOD5E so far, I'm like 99% sure the answer is no. That will be something someone (maybe even one of the writers working on the antagonist-books) will write up and put up on the STV.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably right, which is really unfortunate. W5 really should have the antagonist is playable more than anything since it's supposed to be a reimagining and you can have better motivations for why someone would fall. Be really nice to have compelling villains that you don't agree with but can see why they would do it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495247#post1495247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a couple things that come to mind reading this: 1) He wants WOD5E to go in a different direction than V5 2) He thinks V5 was &quot;neo-noir&quot; and how it was applied was &quot;unfocused&quot; 3) His idea of &quot;Gothic Punk&quot; (as portrayed in H5, I guess) is what he'll be going for with future WOD5E-releases.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard &quot;Gothic-punk&quot; so many times now that is basically has no meaning if it ever did. I find it interesting that he considered V5 unfocused. To me the statement sounds like kind of a ... I dunno a punch down at the previous devs? Like &quot;Oh V5 was so unfocused and wasn't proper Gothic-Punk and I'm updating WoD5 to its proper place.&quot; Which, I guess but, it comes off as a bit full of yourself.<br /> <br /> It just rubs me the wrong way. Especially the following tweet with him saying:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Achilli's Twitter</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In prior editions we leaned into a more Tim Burton-y stylization, but for WoD5 it's more about turning the mood up to 11 and leaving the physical geography the same. Glad that Hunter section did the trick! It's part of that section of cores going forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like is this a way to say without saying that &quot;Old WoD was bad because the style ruined to mood of what gothic-punk is supposed to be&quot;? Don't answer that, Rhetorical Question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T11:22:16-07:00","id":1495256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495249#post1495249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's probably right, which is really unfortunate. W5 really should have the antagonist is playable more than anything since it's supposed to be a reimagining and you can have better motivations for why someone would fall. Be really nice to have compelling villains that you don't agree with but can see why they would do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think villains don't necessarily have to be &quot;compelling&quot; in the sense that you understand them. WtF is a good example. &quot;Angry werewolves constantly going on the hunt&quot; is an overly boring description of WtF but one part that enriches this is a superb rogue's gallery. You have the Pure but then there are plenty of horrifying and weird spirits as well that do strange stuff like fuse with people, for example. Sometimes all you need for a good villain is something that's worth fighting against.<br /> <br /> Since this is a re-imagination, you could of course go into all sorts of directions with what is actually going on with Gaia and the Triad. I mean, was it Revised that first introduced the idea that the Weaver is maybe the true villain? So it's not like WtA hasn't dealt with topics like this before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495249#post1495249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard &quot;Gothic-punk&quot; so many times now that is basically has no meaning if it ever did. I find it interesting that he considered V5 unfocused. To me the statement sounds like kind of a ... I dunno a punch down at the previous devs? Like &quot;Oh V5 was so unfocused and wasn't proper Gothic-Punk and I'm updating WoD5 to its proper place.&quot; Which, I guess but, it comes off as a bit full of yourself.<br /> <br /> It just rubs me the wrong way. Especially the following tweet with him saying:<br /> <br /> Like is this a way to say without saying that &quot;Old WoD was bad because the style ruined to mood of what gothic-punk is supposed to be&quot;? Don't answer that, Rhetorical Question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it just reinforced my idea that he doesn't just want to stealh-ditch old WOD-lore but ditch the whole ST-system as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T13:06:12-07:00","id":1495264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrNatas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1494974-thoughts-on-w5-tribes?p=1495249#post1495249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I've heard &quot;Gothic-punk&quot; so many times now that is basically has no meaning if it ever did. I find it interesting that he considered V5 unfocused. To me the statement sounds like kind of a ... I dunno a punch down at the previous devs? Like &quot;Oh V5 was so unfocused and wasn't proper Gothic-Punk and I'm updating WoD5 to its proper place.&quot; Which, I guess but, it comes off as a bit full of yourself.<br /> <br /> It just rubs me the wrong way. Especially the following tweet with him saying:<br /> <br /> <br /> Like is this a way to say without saying that &quot;Old WoD was bad because the style ruined to mood of what gothic-punk is supposed to be&quot;? Don't answer that, Rhetorical Question.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have a lot of sharp comments fit v5 but I wouldn't call it unfocused. If anything its too focused on what it presumed vtm is 'supposed' to be.<br /> <br /> Personally i don't think Justin's heart is into writtinh wod and that's the issue, I mean v5 sabbat is objectively inferior than revised sabbat which he also wrote -how do you do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-19-2022, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T14:57:59-07:00","id":1495275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Achilli's Twitter</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In prior editions we leaned into a more Tim Burton-y stylization, but for WoD5 it's more about turning the mood up to 11 and leaving the physical geography the same. Glad that Hunter section did the trick! It's part of that section of cores going forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welp, that sort of thinking is not good for WtA. Especially the way things seem to be going for W5.<br /> <br /> You are not playing a cursed being or someone wearing a wolf pelt in WtA. You are not playing a solitary hunter who is cursed to change or a God-blessed creature going to Hell to fight demons every night. You are not playing an astral-projecting person.<br /> <br /> In WtA, you are playing a member of a species of spirit wolves who are tied to the Earth Mother. The main focus of the game is not dealing with being a werewolf unless you modify things. The main focus is fighting the war for Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Aka, the Tim Burtony stuff is the core of the game.<br /> <br /> You want to re-imagine WtA to be more street level and toned down? Make the game about the cursed creature dealing with being monster and the tribes ways to deal with that change. This is something neither WtA or Forsaken (aside from the Chroniclers Guide) does, so it would stand out.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T15:09:58-07:00","id":1495278,"title":"","content":"Justin's heart wasn't in this 18 years ago...<br /> <br /> What bridges Revised Sabbat and V5 Sabbat is Belial's Brood in VtR 1e.<br /> <br /> While the Brood works fine in VtR, you can pretty easily see how all of the &quot;good&quot; parts of playable Sabbat were spread around other places during the VtR reboot, until the Brood was stripped down to the VtM 1e violent shovelhead style of antagonists. How he can make both of those Sabbat books is: he did his best Sabbat book in the 90s, and wants to do different stuff now, but to do the stuff he wants to do, he needs to play ball with Paradox and maintain the legacy brand enough to keep them happy.<br /> <br /> He's been abundantly clear via H5 and the W5 previews that however much he wants to be working in the broad context of the WoD, he doesn't really want to be dealing with any more legacy material than he has to. A lot of the red flags in how the Tribe preview turned out seem to easily flow from him having to balance out the demands of keeping some legacy stuff, but wanting to do a new thing rather than repeat the past.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T15:13:38-07:00","id":1495279,"title":"","content":"One suspicion I have is that the W5-concepts of &quot;Gaia is dead/dying&quot; and &quot;The Get have fallen&quot; are just holdovers from the previous team and Justin has zero interest in that but was forced to keep it in his version of W5. And so any explanations we are gonna get will be paper-thin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}